Here are the complete configuration and documentation files to populate your project root.

---

### 1. `.gitignore`

This ensures secrets, heavy instrument dumps, and local Python cache files never get pushed to your Git repository:

```gitignore
# Bytecode & Caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.pytest_cache/

# Virtual Environments
venv/
env/
ENV/
.venv/

# Environment Variables & API Secrets
.env
*.env
!.env.example

# Large Data & Local Dump Files
scrip_master.json
*.log
*.sqlite3

# IDE & Editor Specific Folders
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store